Ara RVV integration smoke evidence — 2026-10-13 (branch 9-ara-rvv, issue #9)

System: CVA6 (Ara Bender pin pulp-platform/cva6 99eac9a6, target
cv64a6_imafdcv_sv39) + Ara 34bd3bc1, config 2_lanes with VLEN=512.
Note: the scalar sweep evidence is on openhwgroup CVA6 81245a47;
the vector system integrates Ara's pinned CVA6 (same lineage, the
commit our ACT config citations already reference).

Bring-up commands (scripts/ara_docker.sh, native arm64 container):
  make -C hardware bender            # Bender 0.31.0
  make -C hardware checkout          # lockfile deps (bender update
                                      # re-resolves and conflicts)
  make -C hardware apply-patches     # SRAM DPI exports (required)
  make verilator                     # Ara-pinned Verilator 5.047
                                      # (CVA6 v5.008 rejects waiver.vlt)
  make -C hardware verilate config=2_lanes vlen=512
  /repo/sw/ara-smoke/build.sh        # Ubuntu riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc
                                      # 13.2, -march=rv64gcv medany
  hardware/build/verilator/Vara_tb_verilator \
      -l ram,/repo/sw/ara-smoke/smoke.elf,elf

Results:
  verilated model: hardware/build/verilator/Vara_tb_verilator (19 MB)
  smoke (sw/ara-smoke/smoke.c: strip-mined vadd.vv + vfadd.vv over
  64 elements, scalar-checked): exit code 0, 3751 cycles, ~46 kHz
  wallclock simulation speed on this host.
  negative control (expected value off by one): exit code 2.
  Restored smoke re-run: exit code 0, same cycle count.

No Docker memory increase was needed in the end (VM stays
7.65 GiB): the wins were running the container natively on arm64
(the CVA6 Verilator is an aarch64 build), building only Ara's
pinned Verilator from source (~3 min), and using the packaged
RISC-V GCC for the smoke kernel instead of building LLVM.
LLVM-based app flow and ACT vector remain open on #9.
